                <pb facs="0332" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1873p2v3/pg276"/>


                <p>Confidential memorandum for the use of the Commissioners on the part of the
                    United States in the American-British Joint High Commission, Washington, 1871: <list>
                        <label>I.</label>
                        <item>Correspondence between Mr. Fish and Sir Edward Thornton <hi
                                rendition="#italic">preliminary</hi> to the negotiation. (For this
                            correspondence see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, page 263 <hi
                                rendition="#italic">et seq.</hi>)</item>
                        <label>II.</label>
                        <item>The fisheries, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg277"
                                >page 277</ref>.</item>
                        <label>III.</label>
                        <item>Navigation of the Saint Lawrence, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>,
                                <ref target="#pg289">page 289</ref>.</item>
                        <label>IV.</label>
                        <item>Reciprocal trade between the United States and the Dominion of Canada,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg292">page
                                292</ref>.</item>
                        <label>V.</label>
                        <item>Northwest water-boundary and the island of San Juan, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg306">page
                            306</ref>.</item>
                        <label>VI.</label>
                        <item>The claims of the United States against Great Britain on account of
                            acts committed by rebel cruisers, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>,
                                <ref target="#pg319">page 319</ref>.</item>
                        <label>VII.</label>
                        <item>Claims of British subjects against the United States for losses and
                            injuries arising out of acts committed during the recent civil war in
                            the United States, <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref
                                target="#pg362">page 362</ref>.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <pb facs="0333" n="[Map 1]" xml:id="pg-seq-0333-map-1"/>
